# T-M6-8 VLAN-freeze dig: fe_buffer already exposes the two params-page
# fields (+0x54 pointer, +0x58 depletion counter) for the FE per-port
# "5+tnums management index", but nobody had ever dumped what +0x54
# actually points at. Recovered the real vendor layout from NXP SDK
# source in this repo (ASK/patches/kernel/010-ask-fman-dpaa-ehash.patch,
# FmPortSetFESupport): it's a byte-array free-list (cursor byte + packed
# pool-offset bytes + a literal list of free tnum indices + 0xFF
# terminator), not a bare counter. Adds one read-only hex-dump line per
# armed port to fe_buffer so the free-list's live cursor/contents can be
# correlated between a sustaining routed flow and a freezing VLAN flow.
