# CC-ACL-OFFLOAD-PLAN.md Phase 1: silicon-verified 2026-09-05 that patch
# 0109's ethtool-ntuple -> CC-tree bridge produces a genuine hardware HIT
# (two identical TCP transfers, one matching a rule and one not, landed on
# two different real FQIDs: 512 steered vs 287 default-RSS). Investigating
# Phase 1's mask-granularity question (0109 rejects any src-ip/dst-ip mask
# other than all-ones/all-zero, blaming "the KG composite is not
# prefix-aligned") found the real cause reading cc_pack_key() directly: the
# composite IS byte-aligned (bytes 1-4 SIP, 5-8 DIP), but cc_pack_key()
# hardcodes msk[]=0xff for every byte of a participating SRC_IP/DST_IP
# field, silently discarding whatever mask value the caller supplied -
# struct fman_cc_key.src_ip_mask/dst_ip_mask were already declared and
# documented ("prefix-style mask") but never wired through
# struct fman_pcd_cc_hw_key (which had no mask fields at all) into the
# actual match-table byte write. This patch adds src_ip_mask_be/
# dst_ip_mask_be to the hw key struct, passes them through
# dpaa_cc_key_to_hw() (defaulting to exact-match 0xffffffff when unset, so
# every existing caller - ask_vlan_cc.c, 0109's own exact-match rules - is
# byte-identical), writes them verbatim into the CC row's mask bytes in
# cc_pack_key() instead of the old hardcoded 0xff, and relaxes 0109's
# dpaa_cls_validate()/dpaa_cls_reinstall() to accept and forward a real
# mask for ip4src/ip4dst (e.g. 255.255.255.0) instead of rejecting it. No
# NIA/register/graft changes - purely which mask bytes land in the
# already-working match table, so it carries none of the task-pool-leak
# risk a leaf-AD NIA change would (see the 0136/F-108 tfene=RELEASE
# incident this project already hit on this exact silicon). Ports/tos stay
# exact-or-wildcard only, out of scope for this pass. Not yet board-tested.
# Upstream-Status: Inappropriate | Risk-Tier: A
0193-fman-pcd-cc-key-mask-passthrough.patch
